From: kemp233 <kemp233@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] z96a dt: fix otp clock-names for mainline 6.1 clk-rk3568

The OTP node in board DTS uses old clock-names "usr\0sbpi\0apb\0phy"
but mainline 6.1 clk-rk3568 driver registers clocks under the
long names "clk_otpc_ns_usr\0clk_otpc_ns_sbpi\0pclk_otpc_ns\0pclk_otpphy".

Result: devm_clk_bulk_get() returns -EINVAL, otp driver probe fails,
nvmem device never registers, then tsadc (which references
nvmem-cells = <trim_base, trim_base_frac>) fails with
"deferred probe pending" forever. CPU thermal zones never appear.

Fix: change OTP node clock-names to match the new driver.

---
 a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-z96a-laptop-v2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-z96a-laptop-v2.dts
@@ -4351,7 +4351,7 @@
 		clocks = <0x23 0x73 0x23 0x72 0x23 0x71 0x23 0x181>;
-		clock-names = "usr\0sbpi\0apb\0phy";
+		clock-names = "clk_otpc_ns_usr\0clk_otpc_ns_sbpi\0pclk_otpc_ns\0pclk_otpphy";
 		resets = <0x23 0x1cf>;
 		reset-names = "otp_phy";
 		phandle = <0x1b6>;
